---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { calService, calUrl } from "../data/site";

const contact = "nuxy@nuxyautomation.com";
---
<Base title="Policies · Nuxy Automation" description="Refunds, care plan cancellations, terms of service and privacy for Nuxy Automation.">
  <h1>Policies</h1>
  <p class="lead">Plain-language terms for working with Nuxy Automation, a one-person business in Faribault, Minnesota. Questions: <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>.</p>
  <p>Last updated November 9, 2026.</p>

  <h2 id="refunds">Refunds</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Before work starts:</strong> every project begins with a 50% deposit. If you cancel before I start, I refund the whole deposit.</li>
    <li><strong>After work starts:</strong> I refund the part of the deposit that covers work I haven’t done yet. Work already finished is yours to keep.</li>
    <li><strong>At handover:</strong> you pay the other 50% after you’ve seen the work running. If something doesn’t do what the written plan says, I fix it at no charge. One round of changes within 14 days of handover is included.</li>
    <li><strong>Launch watch:</strong> for 30 days after handover, every failure alerts me and I check in with you in writing on day 3 and day 14. Anything my work breaks in that time is fixed at no charge.</li>
    <li>Refunds go back to the card or bank account you paid with, through Stripe, usually within 5-10 business days.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="cancel">Care plan cancellations</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The care plan is $100 a month, billed monthly in advance.</li>
    <li>Cancel any time from the link in your monthly receipt email, or by emailing me. It stops at the end of the month you’ve already paid for, and you’re never charged again.</li>
    <li>Months already paid aren’t refunded part-way.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="terms">Terms of service</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>The work:</strong> what you get is the written plan you agreed to by email. Anything outside it is quoted in writing before I do it.</li>
    <li><strong>Prices:</strong> fixed, in US dollars. Sales tax is added only where the law requires it.</li>
    <li><strong>Payment:</strong> through a secure Stripe payment link or invoice (invoices are due within 7 days). Work starts once the first half is paid.</li>
    <li><strong>Your accounts:</strong> I work as an invited user and never ask for your passwords. You can remove my access at any time.</li>
    <li><strong>Ownership:</strong> once you’ve paid in full, everything I build for you is yours. If the second half goes unpaid, I may pause anything of mine that runs outside your accounts, after written notice; nothing in your accounts is deleted.</li>
    <li><strong>Other companies’ tools:</strong> booking, email and texting services are run by other companies. Their fees, outages and rule changes aren’t mine to control, and I’ll tell you about any cost before you sign up. Every account, key and paid plan is in your name and on your card.</li>
    <li><strong>Responsibility:</strong> my total responsibility for any job is limited to what you paid me for it, and I’m not responsible for indirect losses such as lost sales, including from other companies’ outages or data loss.</li>
    <li>These terms follow Minnesota law.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>What I keep:</strong> what you send me through the contact form or by email (your name, business, contact details and what you’d like help with) and what Stripe needs to send you invoices.</li>
    <li><strong>Payments:</strong> handled by Stripe. I never see or store your full card or bank numbers; Stripe’s <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy">privacy policy</a> covers payment data.</li>
    <li><strong>Your customers’ data:</strong> stays in your own accounts. I use it only to do the work you asked for, and I never sell or share it.</li>
    <li><strong>The contact form:</strong> your answers go to my own server, which saves them and emails them to my inbox. It doesn’t keep your IP address. I use them only to reply about your project and never add you to a mailing list. Requests are deleted after a year unless you become a client; messages flagged as spam are deleted after 30 days.</li>
    <li><strong>This website:</strong> no cookies and no advertising or tracking scripts. It counts visits anonymously: which page, which button (for example “started the demo”), the day, and the site you came from. Nothing you type, no IP address and nothing that identifies you. If your browser sends Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control, nothing is counted. The site is hosted by GitHub Pages, which keeps its own server logs.</li>
    {calUrl && <li><strong>Booking a call:</strong> the booking page is run by {calService}. What you enter there (your name, email, the time you pick and any note) is kept by {calService} under its own privacy policy and sent to me so I can call you. It shows only the times I’m free, never what is in my calendar.</li>}
    <li><strong>Email:</strong> if I emailed you about your website and you reply “unsubscribe”, I never email you again.</li>
    <li><strong>Your requests:</strong> email me to see, correct or delete what I have about you.</li>
  </ul>
</Base>
